<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lyubech</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Liubech</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lyubech is a small town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a> in Chernihiv Oblast, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>. Mentioned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a> under the year 882, it is one of the oldest towns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a> and lay in the land of the Severians. In 1097 it hosted the council of Rus' princes that divided the land among their families.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lyubech.jpg" alt="Lyubech" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Iryna Ch · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%97%D0%B0%D0%BC%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B0_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B0_%D0%B2_%D0%9B%D1%8E%D0%B1%D0%B5%D1%87%D1%96.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
